Description: plugin-db qualification layer: records of OpenMixer plugin sets
 The qualification layer of the plugin database: the plugin-qualify records
 of the plugin sets measured on a reference machine of a host class.
 plugin-qualify-sync takes a plugin from them instead of measuring it, and
 only when every file of the installed plugin hashes as the measured one
 did; any other plugin is measured on the machine as before. The sync
 chooses the set of the machine's class and cell.
 .
 Each architecture carries the sets of its machine classes:
 .
  arm64: the rpi5 class, the zynthian-vangelis set measured on a Raspberry
  Pi 5 with ZynthianOS. Hardware records: measured on the machine's own
  audio interface; the verdicts hold, the figures describe that interface
  and are not compared with the reference tier.
 .
  amd64: the x86-64 class, the fedora44 sets, one per sample rate and
  quantum. Provisional records: measured on JACK's dummy driver without
  real-time priority; the crash, hang and unmeasured verdicts hold, the
  cost, latency and xrun figures are not reference figures.
